event: delta
data: {"text": " That will help me (or a colleague) verify the real production stage rather than assuming.\n\n**On installation scheduling specifically:**\n"}

event: delta
data: {"text": "Per our standard process, installation can only be scheduled after production is completed and delivery has taken place — delivery itself needs to be booked in advance, and the site needs to be ready to receive goods (accessible for unloading, elevator/floor access confirmed if applicable). I can't give you a specific installation date until:\n1. Production status is confirmed as completed, and\n2. Delivery is booked and confirmed\n\n**What I'd suggest:**\n"}

event: delta
data: {"text": "- Share the drawing confirmation date or any order confirmation reference you have, and I'll help verify which stage the order is genuinely at.\n"}

event: delta
data: {"text": "- Let me know your site's delivery conditions (address, floor/elevator access, preferred delivery window) so that once production is confirmed complete, we're ready to move straight into delivery/installation scheduling.\n\n"}

event: delta
data: {"text": "If you have a hard deadline (e.g., other trades moving in, move-in date), flag that now — I'll mark it and route it to our operations team so they can assess feasibility directly with the factory, rather than me guessing a date."}

